"enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdagases I was an Indo-Parthian king of the 1st century CE, a nephew of Gondophares according to his coins.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdal-khan"><span class="enc-name">Abdal Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdal Khan was the Kurdish emir of Bitlis in the mid-17th century, ruling a hereditary principality under Ottoman overlordship.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-ghalib"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdallah-al-ghalib.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah al-Ghalib</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah al-Ghalib was sultan of Morocco from 1557 to 1574, the son and successor of Muhammad al-Shaykh in the Saadi dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-mahdi-billah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdallah-al-mahdi-billah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah was the founder of the Fatimid Caliphate, proclaimed caliph in 909 in Ifriqiya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-barshambu"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah Barshambu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah Barshambu was a king of Makuria in Nubia, a member of the royal house who had become a Muslim while living at the Mamluk court in Cairo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-sad-ibn-abi-sarh"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh was an Arab commander and governor of Egypt from about 645 to 656 under the caliph Uthman, his foster-brother.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-tahir"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdallah-ibn-tahir.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah ibn Tahir</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah ibn Tahir was the most celebrated ruler of the Tahirid dynasty, governing Khurasan for the Abbasid Caliphate from 828 to 845 from his capital at Nishapur.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-ibn-yasin"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah ibn Yasin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah ibn Yasin was a Maliki religious scholar and preacher who founded the Almoravid movement among the Sanhaja Berbers of the western Sahara around the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-jamma"><span class="enc-name">Abdallah Jamma</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallah Jamma was the leader of the Qawasma Arabs on the middle Nile around 1500.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdallahi-ibn-muhammad"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdallahi-ibn-muhammad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abdallahi ibn Muhammad</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdallahi ibn Muhammad, known as the Khalifa, was ruler of the Mahdist State in Sudan from 1885 to 1898.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdalonymus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abdalonymus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Abdalonymus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Abdalonymus was king of Sidon, installed by Alexander the Great in 332 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/abdeen-pala